<title>SPAIN: Spain's Catalans say no 1997 budget deal yet.</title>
<headline>Spain's Catalans say no 1997 budget deal yet.</headline>
<dateline>MADRID 1996-09-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>The government's Catalan supporters Convergencia i Unio denied press reports on Tuesday that the party had already lent its support to the 1997 budget draft now being hammered out.</p>
<p>&quot;There is a firm commitment to talks with the objective that the country has a budget, but there is as yet no agreement for support,&quot; a spokeswoman told Reuters in answer to a query.</p>
<p>&quot;The 'yes' won't be given until the final moment, until the vote in the parliament,&quot; she said.</p>
</text>
